{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"expansive-aromatic-whippet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Observation (2026-11-09, release 0.15.0 at ab534d1b382)\n- In a `make worktree` venv, `python -m twine` fails: No module named twine. twine is only in .github/release-requirements.txt.\n- `python -m build` (isolated, resolving pyproject's `hatchling>=1.27` to the newest hatchling) produced wheel and sdist with Metadata-Version 2.5. The release-pinned twine 6.2.0 rejects both: \"InvalidDistribution: '2.5' is not a valid metadata version\".\n- The release.yml path (fresh venv, `pip install --require-hashes --no-deps -r .github/release-requirements.txt`, hatchling 1.31.0, `python -m build --no-isolation`) produces Metadata-Version 2.4, and `twine check` PASSES both artifacts.\n\n## Impact\nA pre-push local packaging check gives a false failure on a correct tree, and the local artifact differs from what release.yml publishes. The release itself is unaffected.\n\n## Remediation options\nA make target that reproduces the release build (hash-locked venv + --no-isolation + twine check), or an upper bound on hatchling in [build-system].requires.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A documented local command reproduces release.yml's build and twine check, and passes on a correct tree.","id":"07b5-2e8e-caea-4bef","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Local 'python -m build && twine check' fails a correct release: isolated build emits Metadata-Version 2.5, and twine is absent from the dev venv"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794259641612464001,"uuid":"c48acaa8-903f-4df8-b378-49975f2191ff"}